  "provenance": {
    "movie_menu": "The EU-only movie debugger wraps its signed selection to 0 through 4 at native instructions 0800C7F0 through 0800C806 and accesses five eight-byte movie-ID/label records using a shift by three. The actual load bases are in its pools at 0800C834 and 0800C894. Its label strings, display-clearing string, separator and mode name occupy the exact native 0812F6A8..0812F704 range. Each ASCII string is a genuine compiler-defined null-terminated array, with separate verified four-byte alignment between objects. The unique Mode holds the native init/update/exit addresses. Two real interior Thumb function entries are exposed by the existing regional extra-label mechanism; no instructions change.",
    "eu_task": "The EU-only 24-byte record at 09F59130 contains the exact task_frd_pooh ASCII name, the four existing mode_test task callbacks and sizeof(UnkModeTestWork) value 0x170. The 14-byte original name lives at 08896644. US and JP have no corresponding record; this native record is owned alongside the callbacks without speculatively moving their translation-unit boundary."
  },
